{"name":"Caramelised Walnut","hex":"#6e564a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"caramelised","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of caramelise"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/caramelised"},{"term":"walnut","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hardwood tree of the genus Juglans.","A nut of the walnut tree."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a dark brown colour, the colour of walnut wood."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/walnut"}],"entries":[{"title":"Walnut","blocks":[{"text":"A walnut is the edible seed of any tree of the genus Juglans, most often the Persian or English walnut, Juglans regia. They are accessory fruit because the outer covering of the fruit is technically an involucre and thus not morphologically part of the carpel; this means it cannot be a drupe but is instead a drupe-like nut."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Walnuts_-_whole_and_open_with_halved_kernel.jpg/330px-Walnuts_-_whole_and_open_with_halved_kernel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walnut","wikidata":"Q208021"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Inside_of_a_walnut_in_growth.jpg/500px-Inside_of_a_walnut_in_growth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Inside_of_a_walnut_in_growth.jpg/500px-Inside_of_a_walnut_in_growth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Inside of a walnut in growth","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AInside_of_a_walnut_in_growth.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Three-part_Walnut-8283.jpg/500px-Three-part_Walnut-8283.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thum